					// A blank node (or another value that cannot be represented in a SPARQL VALUES clause) makes
					// this and every later block unsafe to push down. The current block and the still-unread source
					// become one invocation-owned local join. The remainder is consumed incrementally by that
					// iteration; never drain an unbounded source merely to discover its tail.
					CloseableIteration<BindingSet> fallbackInput = new PrefixedIteration(blockBindings, leftIter);
